# Unfold the phonons of R-3c AlF3 (the child: the 8-atom rhombohedral primitive
# cell, child/FORCE_SETS of a 2x2x2 supercell) onto the Brillouin zone of cubic
# Pm-3m AlF3 (the parent: 4 atoms with Al at the origin, parent/FORCE_SETS of a
# 2x2x2 supercell). Only the antiphase tilt R4+ condenses, so only GM and R
# fold onto the child Gamma point; every arm of X and of M goes to the F star
# of the child, and the arms of each star are equivalent (one class, a). The
# pseudo-parent cell is strongly compressed (volume -9.66 %): the tilt pulls
# the lattice in while the Al-F bonds keep their length.
crystod-phonon --unfold --child-poscar child/167_PPOSCAR_AlF3 --child-dim 2 2 2 --parent-poscar parent/221_PPOSCAR_AlF3 --parent-dim 2 2 2

