# The setting with the rhombohedral axes a+b, b+c, c+a of the parent. It
# differs from crystod-group's setting -1 -1 0  -1 0 -1  0 -1 -1 above by the
# two-fold rotation W = 0 -1 0  -1 0 0  0 0 -1 of the parent, which is also an
# operation of the R-3c child: both settings describe the same domain, and
# the frequencies, weights, labels and the child GM origin are the same; only
# K = M k differs (the setup block is shown).
crystod-phonon --unfold --child-poscar child/167_PPOSCAR_AlF3 --child-dim 2 2 2 --parent-poscar parent/221_PPOSCAR_AlF3 --parent-dim 2 2 2 --trans-mat 1 1 0  0 1 1  1 0 1 -o phonon_unfold_abc

